    "repository": "OpenPresentation/opf-pptx",
    "commit": "6f6122cb7fb8cb89b17c1bea7981397a27ded8ed",
    "note": "toPptx default output (chartex fallback) for chartex chart types; regenerate only with an owner decision to change the default export The world-category entry (ja-JP) was regenerated for FF-49: the theme cs slot, which the Japanese language does not use, is now empty instead of repeating the latin face; the chart parts are unchanged. Regenerated for FF-62 (chart text is the preview's 12 pt, not 9 pt or the PowerPoint default, in every classic chart part): only chart-part sz values changed; commit is the base the fixture was last regenerated on. Regenerated again for the spec-gap P1 round trip (codex/spec-gaps-roundtrip, on top of FF-62): the OPF_SLIDE_V1 tag now carries the content topology of a root chart payload, so the tag parts, their relationships, content types, presentation.xml customer data and the slide custDataLst lines changed; the chart parts, embedded workbooks, theme and diagnostics are byte-identical to the FF-62 entries (verified part by part against a build of main 90802f3 before regenerating)."
